---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data The Layer Line collects, how advertising and analytics cookies are used, and how to exercise your privacy rights."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]} />
    <header class="prose-page__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="prose-page__lead">Last updated September 1, 2026.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page__body">
      <p>
        This policy explains what information The Layer Line ("we," "us") collects when you visit
        thelayerline.com, and how it's used. This is a general policy template; before launch, review it against
        your actual configuration (which analytics and ad services are enabled, which regions you serve) and adapt
        it with qualified legal advice if you need jurisdiction-specific compliance (GDPR, CCPA, etc.).
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We don't require account creation or collect personal information to read the site. The following may be
        collected automatically or when you choose to provide it:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Usage data</strong> via Google Analytics, if enabled — pages visited, approximate location (country/region level), device and browser type, and referring site.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising data</strong> via Google AdSense, if enabled — Google and its partners may use cookies and similar technologies to serve and measure ads, which can include personalization based on your browsing activity across sites.</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter signup</strong> — if you subscribe, we collect your email address for the sole purpose of sending the newsletter.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact form or email</strong> — if you email us, we retain that correspondence to respond to you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files stored on your device. We use them for basic site functionality, analytics
        (understanding how the site is used, in aggregate), and advertising (via Google AdSense). See the
        <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a> for details and how to control them.
      </p>

      <h2>Google AdSense and personalized advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and
        other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your
        visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet. You can opt out of personalized advertising by
        visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google's Ads
        Settings</a>, or opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal data we hold about
        you, and to opt out of certain data uses. To make a request, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@thelayerline.com">privacy@thelayerline.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We'll update the date at the top of this page when this policy changes materially.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:privacy@thelayerline.com">privacy@thelayerline.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
